		KAREL Menuing System Help Screens

Each screen in this file must be exactly 18 lines long and no more than
81 display characters long (132 characters total).

-- Terminal help screen (position: @210)

  Connect the communications cable from the controller CRT/KB port to the
  serial port you are using on the PC.  (Default port is COM1:)
                           [ Keyboard mapping ]
    PC          Controller                PC          Controller
      F1          F1                        Scroll Lock Hold Screen
      F2          F2                        Shf-F2      Cancel Command
      F3          F3                        ^^C          Cancel Command
      F4          F4                        ^^W          Repaint Screen
      F5          F5                        Up          Up
      F6          F6                        Down        Down
      F7          F7                        Left        Left
      F8          F8                        Right       Right
      F9          F9                        Insert      Select
      F10         F10                       Page Up     Prev Screen
      Alt-X       Exit terminal emulator    Page Down   Next Screen
      Alt-H       Display help screen       Delete      Find        
      Alt-S       Display the setup screens F11         Do        

-- End of Terminal help screen

-- Communications help screen (position: @1426)




  This selection requires the serial communications option on the KAREL
  controller.

  - Ensure that the physical connection between the controller and the PC
    is in place (RS-232-C cable, drop cable, etc.)
  - Start the desired protocol on the controller (DDCMP on C3:, MAP).
  - Start NCP on the desired controller port (C3:, M0:).








-- End comm help screen
-- Editor help screen (position: @01861)



You have not yet selected an editor.  To select an editor, select submenu
"Development Options Setup".  This submenu can be reached from the Main menu
under "Program Development", "Dictionary and Forms Manager", and "General
Setup".  When in "Development Options Setup", select "Default editor".  This
will prompt you for your editor's startup file.  This name can be a .EXE, .COM
or .BAT file.  This file must be on the DOS PATH.  See your DOS reference man-
ual on how to set your PATH.  If you wish to use this editor every time you
enter the KAREL menus, select "Make selected options permanent".  The KAREL
menuing system will store this file name and load it each time you enter the
KAREL menus.

If your editor is a word processor, make sure that you save your files as
ASCII.


-- End of Editor help
